<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T4.st2.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S4.T4.st2.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">
Ablation study on token selection methods.
</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="S4.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Ablation Studies. ‘Spatial’ and ‘Temporal’ refer to spatial and temporal compression, respectively. ‘Merge’ indicates whether the compressed tokens are merged with all tokens.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation of token selection methods.</span>
To demonstrate the effectiveness of our proposed SCC strategy, we compare it with other methods of selecting representative tokens in Tab. <a href="#S4.T4.st2" title="In Table 4 ‣ 4.3 Ablation Study ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ LLaVA-Scissor: Token Compression with Semantic Connected Components for Video LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4(b)</span></a>. In addition to random sampling and uniform sampling, we also used L2Norm to select tokens with higher information density for comparison. Note that in our experiments, we only replace the method of obtaining representative tokens, while the ‘Merge’
operation in Tab. <a href="#S4.T4.st1" title="In Table 4 ‣ 4.3 Ablation Study ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ LLaVA-Scissor: Token Compression with Semantic Connected Components for Video LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4(a)</span></a> is retained for a fair comparison. It is evident that our method based on SCC performs better than other sampling methods.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Impact of similarity threshold <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> and error tolerance <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
The similarity threshold <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> and error tolerance <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> are the key parameters in controlling the accuracy of the connectivity graph, as well as the core variables for managing the token number after compression. In Fig. <a href="#S4.F3.sf1" title="In Figure 3 ‣ 4.3 Ablation Study ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ LLaVA-Scissor: Token Compression with Semantic Connected Components for Video LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(a)</span></a> and Fig. <a href="#S4.F3.sf2" title="In Figure 3 ‣ 4.3 Ablation Study ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ LLaVA-Scissor: Token Compression with Semantic Connected Components for Video LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(b)</span></a>, we discuss how the similarity threshold <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> affects the number of tokens after compression across different benchmarks. Fig. <a href="#S4.F3.sf1" title="In Figure 3 ‣ 4.3 Ablation Study ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ LLaVA-Scissor: Token Compression with Semantic Connected Components for Video LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(a)</span></a> corresponds to <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> values ranging from 0.99 to 0.9, while Figure Fig. <a href="#S4.F3.sf2" title="In Figure 3 ‣ 4.3 Ablation Study ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ LLaVA-Scissor: Token Compression with Semantic Connected Components for Video LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(b)</span></a> covers <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> values from 0.89 to 0.8. It is evident that as the threshold for inclusion in connected components becomes more lenient, more tokens are compressed. Additionally, due to the varying distributions of videos across different benchmarks, the number of tokens under the same threshold <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> varies.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The error tolerance <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> in Eqn. (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3.1 Token Compression via Semantic Connected Components (SCC) ‣ 3 LLaVA-Scissor ‣ LLaVA-Scissor: Token Compression with Semantic Connected Components for Video LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) serves as a trade-off between the accuracy of solving connected components and the computational efficiency. Theoretically, the lower the <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, the more precise the connected components obtained. In Figure <a href="#S4.F3.sf3" title="In Figure 3 ‣ 4.3 Ablation Study ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ LLaVA-Scissor: Token Compression with Semantic Connected Components for Video LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(c)</span></a>, we illustrate how token numbers vary with changes in <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> under different <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> values on MVBench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite>. Since we treat uncovered tokens as separate connected components, as <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> increases, the token number also tends to increase.
It can be observed that when <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is smaller than 0.05, the connected components almost no longer change. This indicates that nearly all distinct semantic regions have been identified and merged. Therefore, we set <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=0.05</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S4.F3.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2506.21862v1/imgs/statistics/threshold_high.png" id="S4.F3.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/470;" width="476" height="470" alt="Refer to caption">
