<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Algorithms Analysis</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Union-Find Data Structure</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Union-Find is an efficient data structure designed to manage and merge disjoint sets. It supports two fundamental operations: the ‘Find’ operation to determine the root of the set for a particular element and the ‘Union’ operation to merge two disjoint sets into one.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In practice, the Union-Find data structure is typically optimized using path compression and union-by-rank. Specifically, path compression flattens the tree structure during the ‘Find’ operation by directly linking all nodes along the query path to the root, thereby reducing the time complexity of subsequent queries. Union-by-rank, on the other hand, attaches the smaller tree to the root of the larger tree during the ‘Union’ operation, preventing excessive growth in tree height. We provide the detailed the Union-Find structure in Algorithm. (<a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ B.2 Results with LLaVA-OneVision 0.5B model ‣ Appendix B Supplementary Experimental Analysis ‣ LLaVA-Scissor: Token Compression with Semantic Connected Components for Video LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Approximate Connected Components Algorithm</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Equipped with the Union-Find data structure, we further leverage it to compute the connected components of a graph, as detailed in Algorithm. (<a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ C.2 Approximate Connected Components Algorithm ‣ Appendix C Algorithms Analysis ‣ LLaVA-Scissor: Token Compression with Semantic Connected Components for Video LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). Specifically, given a graph with <span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">N</span> nodes, our approximate connected components algorithm begins by initializing the Union-Find structure with each node as an individual set. We then sample <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{N}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">N</mtext><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{N}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> nodes from the graph to construct an adjacency list and mark each corresponding edge. For each edge in this sampled graph, a Union operation is performed to iteratively merge connected components. After all edges have been processed, we traverse all nodes and invoke the Find operation to determine the root set to which each node belongs, thereby identifying the final connected components. It is important to note that nodes not covered by the sampled connections are treated as single connected component. Finally, considering the relative positional relationships between tokens represented by the nodes, we sort the connected components based on the node with the highest degree within each cluster.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Approximate Connected Components via Union-Find</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            Adjacency matrix <span id="alg2.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">adj_matrix</span>, error tolerance <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            List of connected components

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leftarrow\texttt{adj\_matrix.shape[0]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">adj_matrix.shape[0]</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leftarrow\texttt{adj\_matrix.shape[0]}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
            Initialize <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{nodes\_flag}[i]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">nodes_flag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{nodes\_flag}[i]=1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="alg2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{uf}\leftarrow UnionFind(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">uf</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{uf}\leftarrow UnionFind(n)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l5.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Create an Union-Find set with n nodes
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{sample\_size}\leftarrow\min(n,\lceil\log(n)/\epsilon^{2}\rceil)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">sample_size</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{sample\_size}\leftarrow\min(n,\lceil\log(n)/\epsilon^{2}\rceil)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
