</div>
<div id="alg2.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l22.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">22:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{uf.batch\_union}(\texttt{all\_x},\texttt{all\_y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">uf.batch_union</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">all_x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">all_y</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{uf.batch\_union}(\texttt{all\_x},\texttt{all\_y})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l22.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Merge subgraphs of all <span id="alg2.l22.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sampled_nodes</span> 
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l23.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">23:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\texttt{sampled\_roots}\leftarrow[\texttt{uf.find}(i)\text{ for }i\in\texttt{sampled\_nodes}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">sampled_roots</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">uf.find</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext> for </mtext><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">sampled_nodes</mtext><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{sampled\_roots}\leftarrow[\texttt{uf.find}(i)\text{ for }i\in\texttt{sampled\_nodes}]</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l23.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Find root for <span id="alg2.l23.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sampled_nodes</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l24.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">24:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{unique\_roots}\leftarrow\texttt{Unique}(\texttt{sampled\_roots})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">unique_roots</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Unique</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">sampled_roots</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{unique\_roots}\leftarrow\texttt{Unique}(\texttt{sampled\_roots})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l24.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Find every unique connected component root
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l25.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">25:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{components}\leftarrow[]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">components</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{components}\leftarrow[]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l26.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">26:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l26.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{root}\in\texttt{unique\_roots}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">root</mtext><mo>∈</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">unique_roots</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{root}\in\texttt{unique\_roots}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l26.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l27" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l27.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">27:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{cluster}\leftarrow\texttt{np.where}(\texttt{uf.parent}==\texttt{root})[0].\texttt{tolist}()" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">cluster</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">np.where</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">uf.parent</mtext><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">root</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">tolist</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{cluster}\leftarrow\texttt{np.where}(\texttt{uf.parent}==\texttt{root})[0].\texttt{tolist}()</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l28" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l28.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">28:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{components.append}(\texttt{cluster})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">components.append</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">cluster</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{components.append}(\texttt{cluster})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l29" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l29.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">29:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l29.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l29.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l30" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l30.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">30:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{remain\_nodes}\leftarrow\{i\mid\texttt{nodes\_flag}[i]=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">remain_nodes</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">nodes_flag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{remain\_nodes}\leftarrow\{i\mid\texttt{nodes\_flag}[i]=1\}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l30.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> In case there are any unconsidered nodes.
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l31" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l31.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">31:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{components.extend}(\texttt{remain\_nodes})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">components.extend</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">remain_nodes</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{components.extend}(\texttt{remain\_nodes})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l31.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Treat unconsidered nodes as independent components
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l32" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l32.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">32:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l32.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">components.sort()</span> <span id="alg2.l32.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Sort by the node ID with the highest degree in each cluster. 
</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Complexity Analysis</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first analyze the computational complexity of finding connected components using the Union-Find algorithm without approximation, i.e., when all nodes are considered. For the Union-Find structure optimized with path compression and union by rank, the ‘Find’ and ‘Union’ operations have an amortized time complexity of <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\alpha(n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\alpha(n))</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the inverse Ackermann function, which is generally regarded as a constant less than 5 in practice <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>. The initialization of the Union-Find data structure takes <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math> time, and performing Union on each of the <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> edges results in an overall complexity of <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(m\alpha(n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(m\alpha(n))</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, for a graph with <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> nodes and <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> edges, the total complexity of identifying connected components using Union-Find is <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n+m\alpha(n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n+m\alpha(n))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In our case, since the graph is represented using an adjacency matrix to encode pairwise similarity among tokens, the number of edges in the worst case is <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{N}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐍</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{N}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐍</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of tokens. Thus, without applying any approximation or sparsification, the overall worst-case complexity for computing connected components becomes <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\mathbf{N}^{2}\alpha(\mathbf{N}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐍</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\mathbf{N}^{2}\alpha(\mathbf{N}))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To further improve computational efficiency, we propose an approximation strategy, in which <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{N}^{\prime}=\min(\mathbf{N},\lceil\frac{\log(\mathbf{N})}{\epsilon^{2}}\rceil)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐍</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐍</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{N}^{\prime}=\min(\mathbf{N},\lceil\frac{\log(\mathbf{N})}{\epsilon^{2}}\rceil)</annotation></semantics></math> nodes are sampled from the total <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐍</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{N}</annotation></semantics></math> nodes. For each sampled node, we compute its connectivity with all <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐍</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{N}</annotation></semantics></math> nodes to identify approximate connected components. As a result, when <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{N}&gt;\lceil\frac{\log(\mathbf{N})}{\epsilon^{2}}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐍</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{N}&gt;\lceil\frac{\log(\mathbf{N})}{\epsilon^{2}}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>, the time complexity is:</p>
<table id="A3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\mathbf{N}^{\prime}\cdot\mathbf{N}\alpha(\mathbf{N}))=O(\min(\mathbf{N},\lceil\frac{\log(\mathbf{N})}{\epsilon^{2}}\rceil)\cdot\mathbf{N}\alpha(\mathbf{N}))=O(\log(\mathbf{N})\cdot\mathbf{N}\alpha(\mathbf{N}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐍</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐍</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐍</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐍</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐍</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐍</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\mathbf{N}^{\prime}\cdot\mathbf{N}\alpha(\mathbf{N}))=O(\min(\mathbf{N},\lceil\frac{\log(\mathbf{N})}{\epsilon^{2}}\rceil)\cdot\mathbf{N}\alpha(\mathbf{N}))=O(\log(\mathbf{N})\cdot\mathbf{N}\alpha(\mathbf{N})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Specifically, when the error tolerance <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is set to 0.05, the overall time complexity of the algorithm reduces to <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log(\mathbf{N})\cdot\mathbf{N}\cdot\alpha(\mathbf{N}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐍</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐍</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log(\mathbf{N})\cdot\mathbf{N}\cdot\alpha(\mathbf{N}))</annotation></semantics></math> once the number of tokens exceeds 1200.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
